stification>' under the checkbox."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the grace bound the MCP SIGTERM handler waits on (its numeric value or the exact source, e.g. the docker stop timeout in autodeploy.sh).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.332,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'waits (within the grace) for that worker to exit and the write lock to be free, then sets should_exit; past the grace it logs a WARNING and exits anyway'","'within the grace' repeated in AC3 with no numeric value or named source"],"finding":"The MCP SIGTERM handler's wait bound 'the grace' is referenced but its value/source is never stated in the plan.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1f7fa619aa8ca05f","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 1 (server side) and AC3","norm_id":"n0ba81d2eda0be41f","priority":0.268,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor must choose how long the handler waits for the worker before forcing exit"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Name the grace as the docker stop grace period from infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh (or a module constant) so the wait timeout is unambiguous.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the disposition per idle_sync outcome: PUSH_PENDING (transient/retryable — marker persists, next tick retries), lock-skipped (transient/retryable), and DIVERGED (retryable-self-heal vs fatal-needs-repair) — and whether a repeated DIVERGED escalates beyond a plain WARNING.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.net-mechanism","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.failure-disposition-contract"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.6937,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'idle_sync logs at WARNING when a run ends PUSH_PENDING (with its reason, such as non-fast-forward), DIVERGED, or lock-skipped'","'reconverge (src/rebar/_store/sync.py:224, which fetches and merges but never pushes)'","ABSENCE: no explicit disposition word (retryable/transient vs fatal/permanent) attached to the DIVERGED or PUSH_PENDING outcome."],"finding":"The idle_sync failure arms name their outcomes (PUSH_PENDING, DIVERGED, lock-skipped) and log them, but the plan does not state each arm's DISPOSITION in recoverable/terminal terms — in particular DIVERGED: reconverge 'fetches and merges but never pushes', so it is unclear whether a DIVERGED tick is retryable (next tick re-attempts and eventually converges) or terminal (needs operator repair), and whether a transient push rejection (PUSH_PENDING, non-fast-forward) is preserved as retryable across ticks.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3b08b80cc85c202e","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2 / step 3 (idle_sync outcomes)","norm_id":"n8eb3a09ae331bdf9","priority":0.2063,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A DIVERGED state logs WARNING every 120s forever with no stated resolution (retry-forever vs operator-repair), masking whether the fork is self-healing — the same silent-persistence class the incident showed."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Make the gauge draining-check-and-hold atomic (or have hold() itself refuse when draining) so a tick cannot start a sync after draining begins, and state how stop_local_sweep's grace accounts for an in-flight idle_sync.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.net-mechanism","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.818,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Each tick checks gauge.draining before gauge.hold(); it stops when draining and holds the gauge while running.'","ABSENCE: no statement that draining-check and hold() are a single atomic operation."],"finding":"The idle_sync tick does a check-then-act on the drain gauge ('checks gauge.draining before gauge.hold()') — a TOCTOU window: the server can begin draining between the draining-check and the hold(), so idle_sync could acquire the gauge and start a push while the SIGTERM handler is trying to retire, delaying should_exit.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb5d750ae37963a1e","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2 ('Each tick checks gauge.draining before gauge.hold()')","norm_id":"necec09e69fb6efc7","priority":0.132,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["SIGTERM arrives; handler sets draining; an idle_sync tick that already passed the draining check calls hold() and runs a full reconverge+push inside the grace window, pushing out should_exit."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how stop_local_sweep and the idle_sync daemon thread are sequenced on SIGTERM (e.g. quiesce/join the idle_sync thread before stop_local_sweep waits on the write lock) so idle_sync's own write-lock hold is not observed as a busy lock or mis-attributed to a sweep worker.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.468,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Step 1: stop_local_sweep 'then waits (within the grace) for that worker to exit and the write lock to be free'","Step 2: idle_sync 'holds the gauge while running' and calls reconverge which at src/rebar/_store/sync.py:261 takes `_lock.write_lock(... attempts=1)`","Step 2 says idle_sync 'stops when draining' but a tick already in progress is not described as interrupted — it would continue holding the write lock"],"finding":"The SIGTERM handler's stop_local_sweep waits for the store write lock to be free, but the new idle_sync daemon thread also acquires that same write lock (via reconverge); the plan does not specify the ordering/quiescing between them, so during drain stop_local_sweep could see the lock held by the server's own in-progress idle_sync tick and either wait out the grace needlessly or mis-attribute lock-busy to a sweep worker.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff32595ad5b717a79","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach steps 1 (Server side) and 2 (Idle-timer sync)","norm_id":"n098ca2eb4d2a6b82","priority":0.132,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["SIGTERM arrives while an idle_sync tick is mid-reconverge holding the write lock","stop_local_sweep polls the write lock, finds it busy (held by idle_sync, not a sweep worker), and either burns grace or logs a misleading holder"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Bound the gauge-held portion of idle_sync (timeout on the fetch/push, or hold the gauge only around the local commit/marker work, not the network round-trip) and state the dependency-failure behavior.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T5b","T5a"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Each tick checks gauge.draining before gauge.hold(); it stops when draining and holds the gauge while running.'","'idle_sync calls reconverge ... then calls push.push_after_commit' — these are remote git operations","No timeout stated on the fetch/push while the gauge is held"],"finding":"idle_sync holds the intake gauge for the entire run — including a network fetch/merge/push to the remote — with no stated timeout, so a slow or hung git remote can block client gates for the duration.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f77776f5a