rtability"],"criteria":["T12"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'A daemon thread started beside start_startup_store_sweep ... runs a new sync.idle_sync(tracker) every 120 s.'","'The work lands as 3 independent Gerrit changes'","AC: 'After merge, the host's mcp-deployed-sha equals or descends from the last merged SHA' — a forward check, not a rollback.","ABSENCE: no flag/canary and no explicit revert/rollback step is named for the new signal-handling or idle-timer behavior."],"finding":"The plan changes runtime behavior of a long-running, blue-green-deployed MCP server (new SIGTERM sweep-stop path, a new 120s in-process idle_sync timer, new logging levels) but states no rollback path and no staged/canary rollout — the behavior reaches the production server via the normal deploy flip.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa069394d31c40d04","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach steps 1-2; Scope ('3 independent Gerrit changes')","norm_id":"n1ea1c76bfe2c82af","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["If the new stop_local_sweep signalling or the idle_sync daemon misbehaves in production (e.g. signals the wrong pid, or holds the gauge and starves intake), there is no named cheap undo other than redeploying a prior SHA."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a Rollback line per change and a note that during blue-green overlap the retiring container may run the OLD sweep code while the new container runs the NEW SIGTERM path — confirm that mix cannot deadlock the shared write lock.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_al